  "name": "Starbarian increases haste by 4% and 6% (#2393)",
  "contract": "Starbarian rank 1 704778 and rank 2 706229 (Spell.dbc, SpellFamilyName 32, passive, no class mask) each carry two self-targeted APPLY_AURA effects: effect 0 SPELL_AURA_MOD_MELEE_RANGED_HASTE (192) and effect 1 SPELL_AURA_HASTE_SPELLS (216), both with DieSides 1 and EffectBasePoints 3 (rank 1) or 5 (rank 2), resolving to 4 and 6. The tooltip of both ranks reads 'Increases your haste by $s1%.' Native path only: AuraEffect::HandleModMeleeRangedSpeedPct (192) calls Unit::ApplyAttackTimePercentMod and AuraEffect::HandleModCastingSpeed (216) calls Unit::ApplyCastTimePercentMod, dividing the swing timer and UNIT_MOD_CAST_SPEED by 1.04 or 1.06. Neither id appears in module source. Fixtures: an untalented control, one fixture that learns only rank 1 and one that learns only rank 2, all the same race, class and level with no ratings. Each rank is therefore measured on its own; how a rank-2 purchase replaces rank 1 in the spellbook is talent-window behaviour and is outside this scenario. Bands are the exact ratio 1/1.04 = 0.9615 and 1/1.06 = 0.9434 widened for float rounding (same shape as the merged Chronomancer haste scenarios).",
  "timeout_ms": 60000,
